{{quotation|[[Spirit Vale|Gorseval the Multifarious]]|We fight together! And we will have our revenge!}}

[[Gorseval the Multifarious]] is  the second boss in the [[Spirit Vale]] [[raid]] wing. It is a soul construct<ref name="Souls">[[Scholar Glenna (Mount Balrior)]]
:'''<Character name>:''' Not the first soul construct we've seen, yeah?
:'''Scholar Glenna:''' Oh! Right! Gorseval.
:'''Scholar Glenna:''' Hard to choose which I'd rather bump into: souls melded in the fires of torment...
:'''Scholar Glenna:''' ...or the spectral amalgam of those deemed unworthy for sacrifice.</ref> formed from the angered [[Bloodstone ghost|ghosts]] trapped within the [[Spirit Woods]].

== Biography ==
=== Early history ===
After establishing a foothold in the [[Forsaken Thicket]] in their exile from [[Kryta]], the [[White Mantle]] ordered their [[bandit]] allies to capture people, and those who were deemed [[magic]]ally potent were sacrificed atop the Maguuma [[Bloodstone]] for dark rituals over two centuries. The bandits of [[Spirit Vale]] left the bodies of the unworthy prisoners to rot in the [[Spirit Woods]]. The [[Elder Dragon]] [[Mordremoth]]'s [[Hearts and Minds|demise]] caused a magical shockwave in 1328 <small>[[Mouvelian calendar|AE]]</small>, however, which hit the Forsaken Thicket and released some of the spirits trapped in the Maguuma Bloodstone.<ref>[[Spirit Vale]]
:'''<Character name>:''' These spirits are old. These people died a long time ago–well before the war.</ref><ref>[[Glenna's Field Journal]]
:They were stopped in their tracks by a huge beast made of frightened, vengeful souls whom I'd later find out were shocked free from the Maguuma Bloodstone. Confused and agitated, they sought revenge.</ref>

The freed [[Bloodstone ghost|ghosts]], having forgotten their cause of death at first, alternated between being confused and scared to becoming angry and bloodthirsty when memories of their suffering periodically returned. The bandits quickly learned not to leave more bodies in shallow graves or piles within the woods as the restless spirits increased in number and attacked anyone they came across. When threatened, the ghosts learned to merge together into a single, monstrous entity which the bandits eventually named Gorseval. Some bandits even thought of entertaining themselves by leaving helpless prisoners in the woods and watch them be devoured by Gorseval.<ref>[[Journal Entry]]</ref>

=== [[Forsaken Thicket]] ===
Later in 1328 <small>AE</small>, a squad of raiders assisting the [[Pact]] ventured into the Spirit Vale in search of a missing squad which the bandits had captured earlier. The raiders encountered Gorseval in the woods and heard it voicing its desire for both revenge and merging the souls of more beings into its mass to grow in power. Gorseval was ultimately defeated after a fierce clash, and the raiders conjectured that the ghosts forming Gorseval might have been slaughtered and bound by the bandit leader [[Sabetha the Saboteur]]. This conjecture was proven untrue later when the Pact discovered more evidence of the bandit and White Mantle activities in the region, however. [[Scholar Glenna]], the raiders' associate, recorded Gorseval's true origins in her [[Glenna's Field Journal|field journal]] for posterity.

=== [[Guild Wars 2: Janthir Wilds|Janthir Wilds]] ===
In 1338 <small>AE</small>, the Pact Commander encountered a being similar to Gorseval—[[Lextalion the Merciless]], another soul construct naturally formed from souls, unlike other soul constructs encountered by the Commander, such as the [[titan]]s forged in the [[Foundry of Failed Creations]].<ref name="Souls"/>

