== Walkthrough ==
=== Overview ===
The [[Legendary Ravenous Wanderer]] has [[Haze-Made Form]] which renders it nearly immune to regular damage. The only way to significantly harm it is by destroying [[Haze Heart]]s. The boss's defiance bar must be depleted to spawn them, and there are two ways to do so: [[Battery-Charged Rifles]], and the [[Jade Behemoth]]. While players attempt to utilise the equipment, the boss will be throwing AoE fields across the central area, raising walls and making shockwave attacks. It will also have a dangerous haze aura while it maintains its haze form, however this and the other attacks serve only as obstacles than any real threat (the haze aura will kill you if stay within it long enough).

Each equipment for depleting the defiance bar requires fully charging a battery before it can be unleashed. As with the previous events, players mounted on {{map icon|siege turtle}} [[Siege Turtle]]s can collect [[Unbound Ley-Line Energy]]—players without a turtle may borrow one from one of the rental NPCs nearby, for free. The [[Jade Wall]]s that the boss summons contain quite a few of the energy orbs, and [[Corrupted Jade]] can also be shattered (but take a few more hits to do so). To deliver their charges to a battery, players must be inside the battery's charge zone. However, any enemies inside this zone will prevent the battery taking charges.

=== Snipers ===
To the west of the boss is a platform where a [[Battery-Charged Rifles|rifle bundle]] can be equipped. The first two skills are ineffective against the boss, but can be used to help shatter jade for turtles to collect ley energy. The third skill, High-Charge Round, does defiance damage to the boss, although it has a 300 second cooldown. Once charged, the battery will create an AoE at the platform edge where High-Charge Round's cooldown will rapidly reduce (becoming effectively ~5 seconds). These shots will drain the battery until empty before allowing it to be recharged again.

=== Behemoth ===
To the east is a Mysterious Shipment. After an initial battery charge it will release the [[Jade Behemoth]] to attack the boss. It will do a set amount of defiance damage (around 35%) before retreating to recharge. 10 seconds after being fully charged, two battery charge zones will appear/reappear. Though both zones must be clear before either can take a charge, both batteries pool the charges. Upon fully charging, the behemoth will be able to attack again.

=== Hearts ===
After utilising any means to deplete the boss's defiance, three [[Haze Heart]]s will be ejected. These land below the sniper platform, outside the exit of the tunnel, and north-east of the boss (towards the behemoth). Players have a short window of time (60 seconds) to destroy the hearts, each of which will damage the boss for every 25% depleted. After all three are destroyed (or the timer expires) the boss returns to the previous phase of depleting its defiance.

Once the boss reaches 0%, any remaining hearts vanish and the boss loses the haze form, collapsing before the players. The boss recovers 5% health, but without its haze form players can easily put a final end to the boss with regular attacks.

